      <abstract>
       <para>System log management in &productname; is primarily handled by the &systemd; journal and traditional plain text files located in <filename>/var/log</filename>. By understanding where logs reside and utilizing built-in tools like journalctl and logrotate, administrators can efficiently analyze system events, troubleshoot issues, and manage disk space by automating log rotation and compression.</para>
